# Show UI in Simulator

After any change that affects the running Expo/iOS app UI, do not end the turn until you have shown the user a **fully loaded simulator screenshot** of the relevant screen.

## Required close-out

1. Confirm Metro `/status` is 200 (restart with `REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=<en0 IP> npm start -- --clear` if needed).
2. Boot/open the iOS Simulator (`open -a Simulator`) with the onTrack app (`com.imtihoss.ontracknow`) or Expo Go as appropriate.
3. Deep-link or navigate to the changed surface (e.g. `xcrun simctl openurl booted 'ontrack://workouts'`).
4. Wait until the screen is fully loaded (no blank/white/error boundary, anatomy art visible when relevant).
5. Capture a screenshot with `xcrun simctl io booted screenshot` and **read the image** so it appears in the reply.
6. If the first capture is a splash, loading state, or wrong tab, wait/retry and capture again before finishing.

## Do not

- End on “reload the app” without a simulator screenshot.
- Hand off a white screen, error boundary, or partial load as the final visual proof.
